This license applies to the Tombstone Map mod (the “Work”), including terrain/world data, world composition, object placement, config files, scripts bundled with the mod, UI elements, images, icons, text, branding, and any included assets.

Permission Granted

You are allowed to:

- Run the Tombstone Map mod on a DayZ server.
- Link to the official Steam Workshop page and include it as a dependency in your mod list.
- Mention Tombstone in a server mod list / credits.
- Record/stream gameplay containing Tombstone.
- Allowed Server Monetization (General Only)

General server monetization is permitted (example: donations, cosmetic perks, priority queue), provided that:

- Access to Tombstone is not sold, paywalled, or restricted to paying users.
- Tombstone-exclusive content/features are not sold or offered as paid perks.
- Priority queue is allowed as long as it does not restrict access to Tombstone content/features.

Prohibited Monetization of Tombstone

You may not:

- Sell, rent, license, or monetize Tombstone or any portion of it.
- Place Tombstone behind VIP tiers, subscriptions, Patreon roles, paid whitelisting, or any paid gate.
- Sell Tombstone-exclusive features, locations, or gameplay advantages as part of a paid package.

Promotion / Advertising Restrictions

- You may list Tombstone in a mod list or credits, but you may not use Tombstone as the primary marketing hook to solicit payments or paid memberships, or imply endorsement/affiliation with the authors.
- No Reuploads / No Repacking / No Mirrors
- You may not reupload, repack, mirror, or redistribute Tombstone (in whole or in part).
- Modpacks must use the official Workshop item via dependency only.

No Derivatives Without Permission

- You may not modify, reverse engineer, decompile, or create derivative works of the Tombstone Map mod without prior written permission from the authors.

Termination

- This license terminates automatically upon violation. Upon termination, you must stop using and distributing the Work.

Permissions / Commercial Licensing

- Commercial use or special permissions must be granted in writing by the authors.

